When confronted with RSA encryption & a small `n`, factorize `n` to find `p` and `q`. Then, compute the modular inverse of `e` modulo `(p-1)*(q-1)` to find `d`, the decryption key. This can decrypt the ciphertext when given in an array, applying the formula `plaintext[i] = pow(ciphertext[i], d, n)` for each element.
